hypothesis: v011 moved full_valid_wp from 0.674179 (3-seed mean) to 0.679986, +0.0058
  at 36 sigma, but it changed the mask AND the reset together, so the gain is unattributed.
  This run isolates them. If it lands near 0.674 the soft mask did the work and the
  reset is inert; if near 0.680 the reset did the work and the mask is inert. Either
  way we learn which lever the Phase B/C distillation teacher should be built from,
  instead of attributing +0.0058 to the wrong mechanism.
change_vs_parent: 'EXACTLY ONE change off gru_v011: loss.mask_model -> null, which
  leaves soft_mask None in chunk_loss so every required row keeps unit weight. Unchanged:
  training.state_reset and inference.state_reset stay at 4000, aux weighted-MSE 0.05,
  EMA 0.999, architecture 2x128, seed 1337, 3-epoch cosine schedule. WHY IT MATTERS:
  every downstream decision depends on the attribution, especially whether the distillation
  teacher should be a pair of masked models (v011-like) or masked plus unmasked for
  ensemble diversity.'
